  "notes": "Modified cash basis city. Governmental lines from the Statement of Revenues, Expenditures and Changes in Fund Balances (p5), Total column. Cash basis roll-forward uses the governmental funds fund balances: 3,382,704 + 2,596,570 - 3,122,819 + insurance proceeds 11,244 = 2,867,699 (transfers in and out of 572,926 offset; Total column prints them blank, amounts summed from the fund columns). The 'Taxes' line 437,429 is split using the Statement of Activities general revenues (p2): property 204,433 + sales 187,462 + motor vehicle 26,498 + NPPD 19,036 = 437,429, which also agrees with the combining schedules (p14, p16, p19). Franchise fees 8,014 sit inside 'Other' on p5. Business-type: enterprise funds (Sewer, Water, Sanitation) from the Proprietary Funds statements (p9-p10), Total column; no single total printed, so totals add operating revenues/expenditures and nonoperating items (see computed); roll-forward 1,444,200 + 861,700 - 849,876 = 1,456,024 on a net position basis. Interest expense 15,049 is a disbursement; operating Miscellaneous 13,118 and Other 9,916 are included in business-type lines below. Balance sheet is the government-wide Statement of Net Position, Total column (Internal balances are blank in the total column). Cash flow statement p11-12 not used (cash basis, proprietary field null). Detail: General Fund combining schedule by department (p14-15, per department), Special Revenue combining schedule (p16-17) for Street, Fire Department, Ambulance and CCC Inn (Community Development, Recycling and TIF columns skipped there as duplicates of the Nonmajor schedule, which is used for them; its Community Development operating/capital split differs slightly from the special revenue schedule, total 62,634 agrees), and Nonmajor combining schedule (p19) for Recycling, Community Development, TIF and Hoferer Trust. All-funds budget schedule (p13) skipped as less detailed. Detail expenditure objects other than Personnel services are not itemized by object. Pool sales tax 40,147 appears in the General Fund Pool column and also as Water fund city sales tax; recorded as printed. Fire fund transfer in 571,055 equals the General fund transfers out net. Read pages 1-19 of 19.",
